.\" neojoy.1 — man page for NeoJoy
.\" In honor of Bill Joy.
.TH NEOJOY 1 "April 2026" "neojoy 1.0.0" "NeoJoy"
.SH NAME
neojoy \- fast, modular Neovim distribution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B NVIM_APPNAME=neojoy nvim
.RI [ file .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B NeoJoy
is a Neovim distribution built for speed, modularity, and security.
It uses
.B NVIM_APPNAME
isolation so it does not interfere with an existing Neovim configuration.
.PP
Named in honor of Bill Joy, who wrote vi, co-founded Sun Microsystems,
and shaped the UNIX tools developers still reach for every day.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Fast startup
Target <50ms. All plugins lazy-loaded via lazy.nvim.
.TP
.B LSP
Mason server management, diagnostics, hover, go-to-definition,
format on save.
.TP
.B Completion
nvim-cmp with LSP, buffer, path, and snippet sources (LuaSnip).
.TP
.B Treesitter
Parser management for Neovim 0.12+. Syntax highlighting and
indentation handled natively by Neovim.
.TP
.B Git
gitsigns in the gutter, lazygit integration, hunk navigation.
.TP
.B Fuzzy finding
Telescope with native fzf sorter.
.TP
.B Themes
Catppuccin Mocha (default) and Solarized Dark, switchable at
runtime via
.B :Themery
or
.BR <leader>th .
Selection persists across sessions.
.TP
.B DAP
Debug Adapter Protocol support via nvim-dap, dap-ui, and
mason-nvim-dap.
.TP
.B Polish
nvim-notify, alpha dashboard, todo-comments, spectre, surround.
.TP
.B Override-friendly
Extend without forking via
.IR lua/config/overrides.lua .
.TP
.B Security-conscious
Pinned plugin versions in lazy-lock.json. No auto-installation
of treesitter parsers.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.SS General
.TP
.B <Space>
Leader key.
.TP
.B jk
Exit insert mode.
.TP
.B <leader>w
Save file.
.TP
.B <leader>q
Quit.
.TP
.B <leader>Q
Force quit all.
.TP
.B <leader>h
Clear search highlight.
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B <C-h/j/k/l>
Window navigation.
.TP
.B <S-h> / <S-l>
Previous / next buffer.
.TP
.B <leader>ff
Find files (Telescope).
.TP
.B <leader>fg
Live grep (Telescope).
.TP
.B <leader>fb
Buffers (Telescope).
.SS Editing
.TP
.B <A-j> / <A-k>
Move line or selection down / up.
.TP
.B < / >
Indent left / right, keeping visual selection.
.SS Git
.TP
.B <leader>gg
LazyGit.
.SS Terminal
.TP
.B <C-\e>
Toggle terminal.
.SS Theme
.TP
.B <leader>th
Theme switcher (Themery).
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
Edit
.I lua/config/overrides.lua
to adjust options and keymaps without forking.
To add plugins, create a file in
.IR lua/plugins/extras/ \(em
lazy.nvim picks it up automatically on next launch.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/neojoy/init.lua
Entry point.
.TP
.I ~/.config/neojoy/lazy-lock.json
Pinned plugin versions (commit hashes).
.TP
.I ~/.config/neojoy/lua/core/
Core configuration: options, keymaps, autocommands, lazy.nvim bootstrap.
.TP
.I ~/.config/neojoy/lua/plugins/
Plugin specifications: lsp, completion, treesitter, git, navigation,
ui, dap, polish.
.TP
.I ~/.config/neojoy/lua/config/
LSP server configuration and user overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.config/neojoy/lua/plugins/extras/
User-added plugin specifications.
.TP
.I ~/.config/neojoy/tests/
TDD test suite (141 tests across 9 sessions).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B Neovim >= 0.12
.TP
.B Git
.TP
.B A Nerd Font
For icons.
.TP
.B make and a C compiler
For telescope-fzf-native.
.TP
.B lazygit
Optional, for the lazygit integration.
.SH INSTALLATION
.nf
git clone https://github.com/ChristopherATarr/NeoJoy ~/.config/neojoy
NVIM_APPNAME=neojoy nvim
.fi
.PP
On first launch, lazy.nvim installs all plugins automatically.
.SS Shell alias (recommended)
.nf
alias nj='NVIM_APPNAME=neojoy nvim'
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Plugin versions are pinned in
.I lazy-lock.json
to specific commit hashes. Updates require an explicit
.B :Lazy update
followed by review and re-commit of the lockfile.
Treesitter parsers are not auto-installed; missing parsers are
installed explicitly by the config function at load time.
